  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-61792",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The number $15%$ (expressed as a decimal) is equal to $0.15.$ Therefore, a decrease of $15%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of:\n\n$$\n1-0.15=0.85\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, the car's value was $7\\,500\\cdot (0.85)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, the car's value was $7\\,500\\cdot (0.85)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, the car's value was $7\\,500\\cdot (0.85)^{3}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the last expression gives\n\n$$\n7\\,500\\cdot (0.85)^{3}≈4\\,606.\n$$\n\nSo the car was worth $$4\\,606$ (to the nearest dollar) after $3$ years.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
